WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.608 --> 00:00:03.610
- [Narrator] Take a Pagan festival,

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:08.572
chariots pulled by bikes, and
a tiny Welsh town, and you get

00:00:08.572 --> 00:00:10.480
whatever this is.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.063
(circus music)

00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:17.889
This story takes place
in the Welsh countryside,

00:00:17.889 --> 00:00:19.666
in the town of Llanwrtyd?

00:00:19.666 --> 00:00:21.010
Llanwrtyd?

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.957
- Llanwrtyd Wells.

00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:25.509
We are the smallest town in the UK.

00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:27.307
- [Narrator] And this
is Lindsay Ketteringham.

00:00:27.307 --> 00:00:28.996
He runs the local hotel in town.

00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:31.401
- [Lindsay] It's called
the Neuadd Arms Hotel.

00:00:31.401 --> 00:00:36.159
The town today is a small
farming community primarily.

00:00:36.159 --> 00:00:38.712
Everybody knows everybody else.

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:43.485
Day-to-day life is generally
pretty quiet around here.

00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:46.855
- [Narrator] Except on event day.

00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:50.448
- The Mountain Bike
Chariot Racing Championship

00:00:50.448 --> 00:00:53.993
is an event that was
conceived to be part of

00:00:53.993 --> 00:00:57.208
a Roman festival that
we hold each January.

00:00:57.208 --> 00:00:59.795
The rules of the race are to get round

00:00:59.795 --> 00:01:01.805
in the fastest time possible.

00:01:01.805 --> 00:01:05.677
The course starts off on
a short tarmac stretch,

00:01:05.677 --> 00:01:09.844
then becomes a rough, stony
road with puddles and bumps,

00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:13.733
and eventually comes back to the finish

00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:16.643
along a tarmac stretch
which has speed bumps.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.683
It's not a simple task.

00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:23.013
We do encourage people to
dress up as the Romans did.

00:01:23.013 --> 00:01:26.462
As you can see, people
enter into the spirit of it,

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:28.361
which is what it's all about.

00:01:28.361 --> 00:01:30.421
- [Narrator] Okay, but
Ben-Hur style bike racing

00:01:30.421 --> 00:01:33.921
isn't everything that this tiny town does.

00:01:36.325 --> 00:01:37.884
- [Lindsay] We do the events

00:01:37.884 --> 00:01:40.566
such as Man versus Horse, Bog Snorkelling.

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.953
- [Narrator] And it all
started back in the seventies.

00:01:42.953 --> 00:01:46.267
Llanwrtyd Wells was the
center of the pony trekking

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:50.432
industry in Britain, and in
the 1970's unfortunately,

00:01:50.432 --> 00:01:53.218
the industry went into serious decline.

00:01:53.218 --> 00:01:56.733
At that point the local
business people started looking

00:01:56.733 --> 00:02:01.459
for ideas to boost the economy,
and came up with the idea

00:02:01.459 --> 00:02:05.124
of running events, things
that were slightly different

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.124
and unusual.

00:02:08.322 --> 00:02:12.802
It's great to see the
success of the events,

00:02:12.802 --> 00:02:15.799
see people enjoying themselves,

00:02:15.799 --> 00:02:18.498
and it's great to be able to share what

00:02:18.498 --> 00:02:21.998
this part of the countryside has to offer.

00:02:22.913 --> 00:02:26.471
The aim is to maintain
the great community that

00:02:26.471 --> 00:02:30.489
we have here, even to help
it grow, but not too much.

00:02:30.489 --> 00:02:33.167
We don't want to lose
our smallest town status.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.250
- [Narrator] Hey, I hear you Lindsay.

00:02:39.254 --> 00:02:41.587
(soft ding)

